load @term/seed/code/number/complex
  find complex

# The bicomplex numbers, the complex numbers doubled by a second commutative square root of minus one, the commutative
# cousin of the quaternions. Where Cayley-Dickson doubling sacrifices commutativity to reach the quaternions, the
# bicomplex doubling keeps it but pays by introducing zero divisors, so they are a commutative ring but not a division
# algebra. They sit off to the side of the reversible tower, a road not taken. The form carries the complex numbers they
# are built from.
form bicomplex
  link source, like complex
